		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>Just the page: the button pad disappears and the whole screen becomes three big targets — tap left to page back, right to page forward, above the page for power. A three-finger tap on the page toggles it too.</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Zen</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<true/>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>zenModeEnabled</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Zen Mode</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>What each gesture does, anywhere on the screen. The two groups below can override the one-finger gestures for the strip above the sheet and the band below it; everywhere else — the page itself included — these apply.

Two gestures may hold the same action. Set one to Nothing to switch it off. If you clear every Toggle Zen Mode binding, zen can still be turned off with the Zen Mode switch at the top of this screen.

The side rocker (Up / Down) steps text size inside a book on this build — holding a side button changes the reading font — and scrolls a screenful elsewhere.</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Gestures</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
